Linux System Configuration Files (from /etc) and Their Purposes 

1. ./dracut.conf              - Configuration file for dracut, used to build initial ramdisk (initramfs) images.
2. ./csh.login               - System-wide initialization file read by csh/tcsh login shells.
3. ./nsswitch.conf.bak       - Backup copy of the Name Service Switch configuration file.
4. ./subuid                  - Subordinate user ID delegation mapping for rootless containers (like Podman).
5. ./magic                   - Custom magic numbers configuration used by the 'file' command to determine file types.
6. ./krb5.conf               - Main configuration file for MIT Kerberos V5 authentication security.
7. ./passwd                  - Database containing local user account details (usernames, IDs, shell, home folder).
8. ./kdump.conf              - Configuration file for the Linux kernel crash dumping mechanism (kdump).
9. ./rsyslog.conf            - System logging daemon (rsyslogd) configuration file for managing system logs.
10. ./shells                 - List of valid, secure login shells authorized for use on the system.
11. ./subgid-                - Backup file for subordinate group ID delegation.
12. ./almalinux-release      - Identifies the specific AlmaLinux operating system version installed.
13. ./man_db.conf            - Configuration file for the man database tool, locating man pages paths.
14. ./.pwd.lock              - Lock file used by user utility tools to prevent simultaneous edits to password files.
15. ./resolv.conf            - DNS resolver configuration file containing nameservers for domain resolution.
16. ./protocols              - Mapping file containing names and numbers for standard internet protocols (IP, TCP, UDP).
17. ./cron.deny              - Access control list of users explicitly forbidden from using crontab scheduling.
18. ./DIR_COLORS             - Configuration file dictating the color schemes used by the 'ls' command for file listings.
19. ./csh.cshrc              - System-wide script executed by every csh/tcsh shell invocation.
20. ./services               - Text database mapping network service names to their specific port numbers and protocols.
21. ./request-key.conf       - Configuration file controlling the kernel's key request routing and handling.
22. ./shadow-                - Backup file of the secure local password shadow file.
23. ./ld.so.cache            - Binary cache containing an ordered list of libraries found in standard library directories.
24. ./group-                 - Backup file of the local group definition file.
25. ./motd                   - Message of the Day; text displayed to users upon successful interactive login.
26. ./GREP_COLORS            - Defines color highlights for grep search matches in terminal environments.
27. ./bashrc                 - System-wide configuration script executed for interactive non-login Bash shells.
28. ./environment            - Configuration file specifying system-wide environmental variables for all processes.
29. ./hostname               - Stores the unique system network name (hostname) of the server/machine.
30. ./xattr.conf             - Configuration for extended system file attribute layouts and behavior.
31. ./DIR_COLORS.lightbgcolor - Alternative color template for 'ls' optimized for terminals with light backgrounds.
32. ./virc                   - Default initialization and configuration commands for the vi text editor.
33. ./hosts                  - Static table lookup file mapping IP addresses to hostnames locally.
34. ./logrotate.conf         - Primary configuration managing periodic cycling, compression, and cleaning of log files.
35. ./filesystems            - Sequential list of file system types that the kernel attempts to probe during mounts.
36. ./vconsole.conf          - Configuration file managing the virtual console keyboard mapping and font setup.
37. ./inittab                - Configuration script for system initialization run-levels (used primarily in older SysV init systems).
38. ./ethertypes             - Hexadecimal mapping translating protocol numbers to standard Ethernet types.
39. ./libaudit.conf          - Controls the operational parameters of the audit logging library framework.
40. ./issue                  - Pre-login banner template displayed on local physical terminal connection prompts.
41. ./login.defs             - Shadows configuration suite for password age limits, ID ranges, and user creation settings.
42. ./exports                - Directories explicitly exposed to network clients via Network File System (NFS) exports.
43. ./printcap               - Printer capability database mapping localized printers and print server configs.
44. ./system-release-cpe     - Structured CPE (Common Platform Enumeration) string representing the system release version.
45. ./passwd-                - Backup copy of the local human-readable user database file.
46. ./trusted-key.key        - Contains system trusted encryption cryptographic keys or signature certificates.
47. ./locale.conf            - Defines global locale settings including language, character encoding, and measurements.
48. ./crontab                - System-wide schedule matrix executing periodic automation routines and scripts.
49. ./sysctl.conf            - Kernel configuration interface utilized to fine-tune active operating parameters at runtime.
50. ./sestatus.conf          - Configuration manager for SELinux (Security-Enhanced Linux) status displays.
51. ./issue.net              - Pre-login notification message presented to incoming remote telnet or SSH clients.
52. ./sudo-ldap.conf         - Integrates privileged user sudo commands via remote centralized LDAP query directories.
53. ./chrony.keys            - Pre-shared authentication keys used to validate time updates inside chrony NTP daemons.
54. ./.updated               - Tracking timestamp file recording when the operating system configuration was last updated.
55. ./subgid                 - Maps subordinate group delegation allocations allowing rootless container environments.
56. ./inputrc                - Custom initialization file managing terminal command line keystroke mappings (Readline).
57. ./shadow                 - Encrypted password storage vault separating user password strings from standard access.
58. ./gshadow-               - Backup container file of the local secure group shadow definitions.
59. ./group                  - Defines local security group assignments and identifies member names.
60. ./nsswitch.conf          - Coordinates Name Service Switch lookup order rules across hosts, passwd, and group files.
61. ./sudoers                - Definitive security manifest determining which users hold administrative sudo command rights.
62. ./anacrontab             - Controls anacron tool timings for irregular desktop/laptop system automation cycles.
63. ./machine-id             - Globally unique persistent string identifier generated locally during OS installation.
64. ./adjtime                - State storage text tracking adjustments and drift correction of the system hardware clock.
65. ./ld.so.conf             - Lists directories search paths scanned by the dynamic linker to discover shared libraries.
66. ./subuid-                - Backup log file recording rootless container subordinate user delegation details.
67. ./profile                - System-wide shell setup script parsing configurations upon initial user login execution.
68. ./sudo.conf              - Plugin configuration management interface for the sudo security subsystem.
69. ./aliases                - Dynamic lookup index directing mail forwarding aliases under system MTA engines.
70. ./chrony.conf            - Central configuration file managing the chrony NTP client/server time daemon.
71. ./networks               - Legacy address translation library containing descriptive local network strings.
72. ./fstab                  - System filesystem mounting matrix mapping physical storage targets to operational paths.
73. ./gshadow                - Encrypted storage housing administrative passwords and access values for system groups.
74. ./libuser.conf           - Common operational defaults utilized by the libuser library tool suite.
75. ./makedumpfile.conf.sample - Sample setup script managing core exclusions for the kdump memory output optimization.
76. ./rpc                    - Portmapper numerical conversion table defining ONC RPC program configurations.
77. ./mke2fs.conf            - Default format blueprints used when instantiating new ext2/ext3/ext4 file systems.
78. ./crypttab               - Encrypted block storage target definition file mapped early during OS boot phases.
79. ./host.conf              - System resolver parameters file managing network domain name lookup rules.

Note: I've made this doc based on Almalinux 9.
